 “och först pröva ett halvår med både telefon och webb.” / “Öppna beslut föreslår ett sex månader långt försök i alla sju lokaler, med båda bokningsvägarna kvar.” | Supported order, duration, and simultaneous channels. Recommendation, not claim that a trial already exists. |\n| “The pilot does not measure digital familiarity” | “Rapporten räknar bokningar, inte unika personer. Den mäter inte ålder, funktionsförmåga eller digital vana.” | Digital familiarity appropriately conveys digital vana. The draft changes the report's absence of measurement to an absence throughout the pilot. Finding F3. |\n| “The municipality’s pilot report, Bokning av föreningslokaler, dated April 8, 2026” | “Kommunens pilotrapport Bokning av föreningslokaler, 8 april 2026” | Ownership, document title, and date supported. Swedish report title retained without inventing an English official title. |\n| “records 96 web bookings and 24 phone bookings during an eight-week trial in two venues.” | “gäller ett åtta veckor långt försök i två lokaler. Under försöket gjordes 96 bokningar via webb och 24 via telefon.” | Both counts are attributed to the named report. Channel, units, duration, and two-premises scope preserved. No assessment that the count is high or low is added. |\n| “These are bookings, not unique people.” | “Rapporten räknar bokningar, inte unika personer.” | Supported explanation of the preceding report figures. “These” refers to those figures. |\n| “The report does not measure age, functional ability, or familiarity with digital technology.” | “Den mäter inte ålder, funktionsförmåga eller digital vana.” | Subject and three measurement omissions preserved. English terms name the attributes at issue in this context. |\n| “Those 24 phone bookings cannot establish what proportion of residents cannot book online.” | “Under försöket gjordes 96 bokningar via webb och 24 via telefon. Rapporten räknar bokningar, inte unika personer. Den mäter inte ålder, funktionsförmåga eller digital vana. Telefonbokningarna kan därför inte användas för att säga hur stor andel av invånarna som inte kan boka digitalt.” / “Att en bokning går via telefon är inte ett bevis för att någon inte kan använda webben.” | The specific count and inability to infer a population share are supported. Although “online” is narrower than “digital,” the additional supplied web-specific statement independently supports the inability-to-infer claim about web booking. It does not present a share or claim anyone's actual inability. No defect. |\n| “A phone booking is a reason to ask why that channel is used, not proof that someone cannot use the web.” | “Sanna Eks ståndpunkt: ‘Att en bokning går via telefon är inte ett bevis för att någon inte kan använda webben. Det är ett skäl att ta reda på varför telefonen fortfarande används.’ Detta får citeras eller refereras.” | Supported paraphrase of Sanna's position with inference/proof distinction intact. “That channel” identifies phone booking. The draft omits “still,” adding no historical claim. |\n| “The workload argument needs a measurement” | “Någon tidsmätning eller ekonomisk besparingsberäkning finns inte i handlingarna.” / “Hon menar att kommunen först måste kunna väga arbetskostnaden mot värdet för användarna.” | Supported author's judgment about the adequacy of the decision material. Not presented as an independent legal or technical requirement. |\n| “The staff report gives a concrete reason for removing phone access: avoiding the work of entering information through two workflows.” | “Motivet i utlåtandet är att personalen ska slippa föra in uppgifter i två flöden. … Förvaltningens verkliga invändning mot att behålla båda kanalerna är dubbel administration, inte att telefonanvändare är lata eller dyra.” | Actual attributed administrative rationale preserved. “Phone access” means access to phone booking in this paragraph's context. No unsupported motive, cost estimate, or achieved saving is added. |\n| “That administrative concern deserves an answer.” | “Förvaltningens verkliga invändning mot att behålla båda kanalerna är dubbel administration” / “Hon menar att kommunen först måste kunna väga arbetskostnaden mot värdet för användarna.” | Supported author evaluation. |\n| “But the documents contain no time measurements or calculation of financial savings.” | “Någon tidsmätning eller ekonomisk besparingsberäkning finns inte i handlingarna.” | Absence confined to the documents, as in the source. Financial calculation is not confused with actual achieved savings. |\n| “An unmeasured workload is an inadequate basis for a permanent switch.” | “Någon tidsmätning eller ekonomisk besparingsberäkning finns inte i handlingarna.” / “Tes: kommunstyrelsen bör skjuta upp ett permanent byte till enbart digital bokning av föreningslokaler” | “Inadequate basis” is supported author criticism. “Unmeasured” extends absence in the documents into absence of measurement itself. Finding F5. |\n| “I do not oppose digital booking” | “Hon motsätter sig inte digital bokning.” | The source author's explicit position is preserved in first person, without weakening or intensifying it. |\n| “the board must first be able to weigh the labor cost against the value to users.” | “Hon menar att kommunen först måste kunna väga arbetskostnaden mot värdet för användarna.” | Supported Sanna position. Board specification is consistent with the source's expressly assigned decision maker. “Must” retains the standpoint's strength; not asserted as law. |\n| “The board should authorize a trial and assess its cost” | “Öppna beslut föreslår ett sex månader långt försök i alla sju lokaler, med båda bokningsvägarna kvar.” / “Kostnaden behöver kommunstyrelsen ta ställning till.” | Supported advocacy for adoption of the association proposal and board cost consideration. No numerical cost or existing appropriation asserted. |\n| “Öppna beslut proposes keeping both booking routes for six months at all seven venues.” | “Öppna beslut föreslår ett sex månader långt försök i alla sju lokaler, med båda bokningsvägarna kvar.” | Proposer, proposal status, scope, duration, and routes preserved. |\n| “Staff should record the time spent on each route” | “Under försöket ska förvaltningen registrera tidsåtgång per bokningsväg” | Proposal's requested action preserved. Staff appropriately represents the administration implementing it. The preceding six-month-trial sentence establishes the timing. |\n| “and ask users to say voluntarily why they choose phone or web.” | “och be användarna frivilligt ange varför de väljer telefon eller webb.” | Users, voluntary disclosure, choice question, and channels preserved. No demand that they identify themselves or demonstrate inability is added. |\n| “Our association makes no claim to have funded the trial or estimated its cost.” | “Föreningen gör inget anspråk på att ha finansierat eller kostnadsberäknat försöket.” | Supported absence of a claim. The draft correctly does not turn this into a categorical assertion that funding or costing never occurred. First-person collective is valid for the association's named spokesperson. |\n| “The municipal executive board should postpone the permanent switch, assess the trial’s cost, and authorize it.” | “Tes: kommunstyrelsen bör skjuta upp ett permanent byte till enbart digital bokning av föreningslokaler och först pröva ett halvår med både telefon och webb.” / “Kostnaden behöver kommunstyrelsen ta ställning till.” | Supported author advocacy naming concrete board actions. No claim that cost is known, low, funded, or irrelevant. “It” refers to the proposed trial. |\n| “Afterward, it can decide whether to remove, change, or retain a booking channel.” | “Därefter kan den avgöra om en kanal ska tas bort, ändras eller behållas.” / “och först pröva ett halvår med både telefon och webb.” | Decision maker, possible decisions, and later timing supported. The draft preserves the open outcome, rather than implying a necessary removal. |\n\n## Pronoun, person, number, and natural-gender accounting\n\n| Draft form | Supplied support | Assessment |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| “I” in “I urge” and “I do not oppose” | “Avsändare är Sanna Ek, talesperson för föreningen Öppna beslut.” / “Sanna Eks ståndpunkt” / “Hon motsätter sig inte digital bokning.” | First-person singular speech by the named author is supported. English “I” asserts no natural gender. Source “hon” is third-person feminine singular; the draft neither invents nor contradicts that gender. |\n| “Our association” | “Avsändare är Sanna Ek, talesperson för föreningen Öppna beslut.” / “Föreningen gör inget anspråk …” | The spokesperson's first-person collective identification with the named association is supported. “Our” denotes the collective; it does not add the number or gender of particular members. |\n| “users … they” | “användarna … varför de väljer telefon eller webb” | Both refer to plural users. English singular “they” is not involved here. Neither “användarna” nor “de” gives the users' natural gender. Swedish common grammatical gender of the noun is not male natural gender. |\n| “someone” | “någon inte kan använda webben” | Indefinite singular person preserved; neither form specifies natural gender. |\n| “it” in “authorize it” | “ett sex månader långt försök” | Singular trial, not a person. Swedish neuter grammatical gender and English impersonal pronoun introduce no natural-gender claim. |\n| “it” in “Afterward, it can decide” | “Kostnaden behöver kommunstyrelsen ta ställning till. Därefter kan den avgöra …” | Singular institutional board preserved. Swedish “den” is grammatical common gender here, not a human natural-gender assertion. |\n| “These”; “Those”; “that channel”; “That administrative concern” | The immediately preceding report counts, “telefonen,” and “dubbel administration” | Demonstrative references are supported and do not convey human gender. The first two refer to plural booking/count referents; the latter two to singular nonhuman referents. |\n\n## Source-support findings and smallest supported repairs\n\n### F1 — Added locality of the associations\n\nDraft: “two venues for local associations” and “all seven venues for local associations.”\n\nSource: “föreningslokaler” and “alla sju lokaler.” The source identifies association premises, but does not locate or restrict the associations themselves.\n\nDifference: geographical scope of the beneficiaries. A municipality could offer association premises to nationwide associations with no local membership or branch. That remains compatible with every supplied statement and satisfies the source term while failing the draft's added description. Conversely, premises intended for local associations are association premises, so that direction does not produce a counterexample. No supplied statement excludes the standing case.\n\nSmallest repair: replace “venues for local associations” with “association venues” in both occurrences.\n\n### F2 — The summary changes the counting subject\n\nDraft: “An eight-week pilot … counted bookings rather than individual users.”\n\nSource: “Rapporten räknar bokningar, inte unika personer.”\n\nDifference: subject and scope. The pilot could have collected a distinct-user count in an internal dataset while the published report counted only bookings. The source holds and the draft's characterization of the pilot as counting bookings rather than users fails. Conversely, a pilot could collect bookings only while a report additionally reconstructs a unique-person count; the draft would hold while the source's report-only-count statement would fail. These are tests of the semantic scopes, not allegations about what occurred. Nothing supplied excludes the first case.\n\nSmallest repair: “The report on an eight-week pilot in two association venues counted bookings rather than unique people.”\n\n### F3 — The heading turns a report limitation into a pilot-wide absence\n\nDraft heading: “The pilot does not measure digital familiarity.”\n\nSource