t gap\n\nDraft: “An unmeasured workload is an inadequate basis for a permanent switch.”\n\nSource: “Någon tidsmätning eller ekonomisk besparingsberäkning finns inte i handlingarna.”\n\nDifference: location and scope of absence. Staff could have measured the workload in a notebook or internal timesheet without including any time measurements in the decision documents. The source would hold while the workload would not be “unmeasured.” Conversely, the documents could include measurements of some different task while the two-route workload remained unmeasured; the draft's workload description could hold while the source's document-wide absence would fail. No supplied statement excludes the standing first case. The inadequacy judgment itself is supported advocacy and should remain sharp.\n\nSmallest repair: “A workload argument without time measurements in the decision documents is an inadequate basis for a permanent switch.”\n\n## Translation findings\n\nNo direct speech is quoted, so no separate quoted-speech translation finding applies. The digital/online scope change in F4 and the added locality in F1 are meaning changes outside quoted speech and are recorded above as source-support findings. Other terminology and first-person reframing preserve the supplied meaning in this context.\n\n## Completion status\n\nComplete: the entire draft, headings, summary, attribution, body, pronouns, and implications have been compared with all supplied material. The draft and source were not changed. Unresolved source-support findings: F1, F2, F3, F4, and F5. No unresolved separate quotation-translation findings.\n"}"}], "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"turn_id": "01a0f770-3b92-7493-b6a2-035e600daa81", "create_time": 1790858332.6573}}}
